  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.4.0: Opt-in QoS scheduling. FIFO stays the default; pass a QoSKit queue (TaskQueue(IQoSQueue<TaskDetails>) or TaskQueueOptions.Scheduler) to start tasks by strict priority with aging, weighted fairness per tenant, and other disciplines, with the scheduler providing capacity and overflow policy. MaxConcurrentTasks can now be changed on a live queue; MaxQueueSize changes after first use throw instead of being ignored. Adds a QoSKit dependency. v2.3.0: Lifecycle fixes. Stop() retains unstarted tasks (they run after the next Start()) and tasks can be added while stopped; Dispose() completes every unstarted task as canceled (handles canceled, OnTaskCanceled fired) instead of hanging; each task raises exactly one terminal event; OnProcessingStopped fires once; Stop(guid) cancels queued tasks; adding after dispose throws ObjectDisposedException; StopAsync(waitForCompletion) and IsRunning fixed; fixed a hang when disposing with a task waiting for a slot. v2.2.0: Added built-in observability. TaskQueue and TaskRunWithTimeout emit OpenTelemetry-shaped metrics and traces through the BCL Meter and ActivitySource named TaskHandler (queue depth, concurrency in use, per-stage durations, outcomes, rejections, cancellations, errors by type), with trace context propagated from enqueue into task code. New TaskQueue.Name and TaskQueueOptions.Name label each queue. No new runtime dependency on net8.0+; netstandard targets add System.Diagnostics.DiagnosticSource. See TELEMETRY.md. v2.1.1: Fixed result-returning EnqueueAsync<T> overloads so that a task exceeding its timeout completes the TaskHandle<T> with a TimeoutException (previously it double-completed the handle, surfacing a cancellation plus an InvalidOperationException fault). Hardened TaskHandle<T> completion to be idempotent. Updated System.Threading.Channels and Microsoft.Bcl.AsyncInterfaces to 10.0.11. v2.1.0: Retargeted to net8.0 and net10.0 (dropped net6.0); still supports netstandard2.0 and netstandard2.1. v2.0.0: Event-driven architecture (10-100x faster), async API (StartAsync, StopAsync, DisposeAsync), task results (TaskHandle<T>), priorities, timeouts, statistics, progress reporting. BREAKING: Removed IterationDelayMs and QueuedTasks properties.",
